# Authentik: MCP only

Anything Authentik (users, groups, apps, OAuth2/OIDC providers, flows, blueprints, tokens, policies, outposts) goes through **`user-authentik` MCP**. Do not use the Authentik admin UI, `curl` to `/api/v3`, or Coolify container logs as a substitute for Authentik API reads/writes.

## How

`GetMcpTools` on `user-authentik` first, then `CallMcpTool`. Name matches the object: `authentik_users_*`, `authentik_groups_*`, `authentik_apps_*`, `authentik_providers_*` / `authentik_providers_by_type_*`, `authentik_flows_*`, `authentik_blueprints_*`, `authentik_tokens_*`.

```text
❌ BAD  open https://authentik.../if/admin / curl -H "Authorization: Bearer …" …/api/v3/providers/oauth2/
✅ GOOD GetMcpTools({ server: "user-authentik" }) then authentik_providers_list / authentik_apps_list / authentik_users_list
```

Need a schema: fetch that one tool, then call. Auth failure: `mcp_auth` on `user-authentik`, inspect, retry once.

## Boundaries

- Coolify deploys the Authentik *stack*. Authentik *config* (provider, app, groups, blueprint apply) is this MCP, not Coolify.
- Clared app DB is not Authentik. Schema/SQL for Coolify Postgres is dbhub, not Authentik MCP.
- Do not paste production client secrets into repo files. Read via MCP; leave SECRET in Coolify env.
